WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.260
Why do cyclones spin anticlockwise

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.511
in the north,

3
00:00:03.511 --> 00:00:05.782
and clockwise in the south?

4
00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:08.136
The Earth's rotation deflects moving

5
00:00:08.136 --> 00:00:09.558
air. To the right in

6
00:00:09.558 --> 00:00:10.873
the northern hemisphere,

7
00:00:10.873 --> 00:00:11.882
and to the left in

8
00:00:11.882 --> 00:00:13.104
the southern.

9
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.370
At the equator,

10
00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.689
the force is zero.

11
00:00:15.689 --> 00:00:18.187
That's why tropical cyclones rarely

12
00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:20.219
form within about 5 degrees

13
00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:21.267
of it.

14
00:00:21.935 --> 00:00:23.378
It explains the direction of

15
00:00:23.378 --> 00:00:25.367
the trade winds and westerlies,

16
00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.619
and the spin of cyclones.

17
00:00:27.966 --> 00:00:29.137
Your turn.

18
00:00:29.137 --> 00:00:31.092
Where is it greatest?
